                <pb facs="0549" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg455"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701. 4112/90: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Mexico</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-21T20:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 21, 1924—8
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>326. Your 228, June 20, 3 p.m. Department assumes that Cummins is now eh route to
                    Laredo and therefore representations directed in Department’s 319, June 19, 7
                    p.m. apparently need not be made. However, Department depends upon your
                    discretion in case of emergency before Cummins leaves Mexican soil.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
